The Torrey topic-label `"Herbs, & C"` (and the junk label `"The gate of, a hanging of blue, purple, &c twenty cubits wide..."`) are stored raw with `&` in the source .py files (confirmed: 61 occurrences across 18 files, e.g. exo.py line 895: `"appears under: Children, Egypt, Herbs, & C, ..."`) but are stored as `&amp;` in the base HTML because inject.py runs them through html_sanitize.sanitize_html which calls _escape_text (html_sanitize.py:464-465). Searching base_texts for the raw old_body (`& C`) finds 0 matches → the body is silently counted as `base_miss` (source-only) and the base HTML is not updated. Confirmed: base HTML has `&amp; C` (26 files, 61 occurrences) while source has raw `& C`. The same pattern applies to the second junk topic containing `&c`. Contrast: _reingest_eastons.py uses `escape=True` when building the new body so old-body vs source is consistent, and source .py Easton bodies never contain raw `&`.

